      "content": "[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GPT 5.5 biosafety bounty\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenAI announced a biosafety bounty for GPT 5.5, offering rewards for identifying potential safety issues in biological applications of the model. Hacker News discussion highlights community concerns about AI safety.\",\n    \"author\": \"OpenAI (discussed on Hacker News)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40385621\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"AI safety\", \"GPT-5.5\", \"biosafety\", \"bounty programs\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Show HN: A Karpathy-style LLM wiki your agents maintain\",\n    \"description\": \"GitHub project showcasing a Karpathy-style LLM wiki that AI agents maintain automatically using Markdown and Git, demonstrating agentic systems that can self-document and update knowledge bases.\",\n    \"author\": \"nex-crm (discussed on Hacker News)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40384567\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"LLM\", \"documentation\", \"Git\", \"agentic systems\", \"Karpathy\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Open source memory layer so any AI agent can do what Claude.ai and ChatGPT do\",\n    \"description\": \"Open source project implementing a memory layer for AI agents, providing persistent memory capabilities similar to Claude.ai and ChatGPT. Discussion on Hacker News explores approaches to agent memory.\",\n    \"author\": \"alash3al (discussed on Hacker News)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40383901\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"memory\", \"open source\", \"Claude\", \"ChatGPT\", \"agent infrastructure\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Lambda Calculus Benchmark for AI\",\n    \"description\": \"Project proposing Lambda Calculus as a benchmark for AI reasoning capabilities, discussed on Hacker News as a way to test fundamental computational reasoning in language models.\",\n    \"author\": \"victortaelin (discussed on Hacker News)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40385123\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-26\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI benchmarks\", \"Lambda Calculus\", \"reasoning\", \"LLM evaluation\", \"theoretical CS\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Google plans to invest up to $40B in Anthropic\",\n    \"description\": \"Bloomberg report discussing Google's planned $40B investment in Anthropic, highlighting the intensifying AI arms race and big tech's bet on Anthropic as an AI leader. Extensive Hacker News discussion.\",\n    \"author\": \"Bloomberg (discussed on Hacker News)\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40379245\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"Google\", \"AI investment\", \"funding\", \"big tech\", \"AI race\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek V4—almost on the frontier, a fraction of the price\",\n    \"description\": \"Chinese AI lab DeepSeek released V4 series preview models (DeepSeek-V4-Pro and DeepSeek-V4-Flash). Simon Willison analyzes their performance and pricing positioning as near-frontier models at significantly lower costs than Western competitors.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/deepseek-v4/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"AI pricing\", \"Chinese AI\", \"model releases\", \"DeepSeek\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Claude Code quality postmortem: agentic systems are fragile\",\n    \"description\": \"Anthropic published a postmortem on Claude Code quality issues. Three separate harness bugs (not model issues) caused problems, including a bug that cleared thinking context every turn instead of once. Simon highlights the complexity of building agentic systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/claude-code-quality/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"coding agents\", \"AI safety\", \"system design\", \"postmortem\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Honker: Postgres NOTIFY/LISTEN semantics for SQLite\",\n    \"description\": \"A Rust SQLite extension implementing transactional outbox pattern for SQLite, enabling queue and stream semantics with NOTIFY/LISTEN-style functionality. Uses WAL mode polling for near-real-time updates.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/honker/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"SQLite\", \"databases\", \"queues\", \"transactional outbox\", \"Rust\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Bluesky's For You feed: 72K users on a gaming PC\",\n    \"description\": \"spacecowboy's Bluesky For You feed serves 72,000 users from a single Go process on a gaming PC (16 cores, 96GB RAM, 4TB NVMe) with SQLite storing 90 days of data (419GB). Total cost: $30/month. Could theoretically scale to all 1M Bluesky users.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing spacecowboy)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/bluesky-for-you/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"SQLite\", \"scaling\", \"Go\", \"Bluesky\", \"architecture\", \"cost efficiency\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Tool Attention Is All You Need: Dynamic Tool Gating for Agentic Workflows\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper proposing 'Tool Attention' mechanism with dynamic tool gating and lazy schema loading to eliminate the MCP/tools tax in scalable agentic workflows, addressing performance overhead in tool-using AI agents.\",\n    \"author\": \"Anuj Sadani, Deepak Kumar\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21816\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"agentic workflows\", \"tool use\", \"MCP\", \"LLM optimization\", \"arXiv\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"From Research Question to Scientific Workflow: Agentic AI for Science Automation\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper exploring leveraging agentic AI to automate scientific workflows from research question to execution, potentially transforming how scientists conduct research by automating complex multi-step processes.\",\n    \"author\": \"Bartosz Balis, Michal Orzechowski, Piotr Kica, Michal Dygas, Michal Kuszewski\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21910\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"scientific automation\", \"research workflows\", \"agentic AI\", \"arXiv\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Separable Expert Architecture: Privacy-Preserving LLM Personalization\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper proposing a separable expert architecture for privacy-preserving LLM personalization via composable adapters and deletable user proxies, addressing privacy concerns in personalized AI systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Chris Schneider, Philipp Schoenegger, Ben Bariach\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21571\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"LLM personalization\", \"privacy\", \"adapters\", \"model architecture\", \"arXiv\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Thinking with Reasoning Skills: Fewer Tokens, More Accuracy\",\n    \"description\": \"Paper proposing methods to achieve higher accuracy with fewer tokens by focusing on reasoning skills, suggesting efficiency improvements in LLM inference for ACL 2026 Industry Track.\",\n    \"author\": \"Guangxiang Zhao, Qilong Shi, Xusen Xiao, Xiangzheng Zhang, Tong Yang, Lin Sun\",\n    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21764\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"LLM efficiency\", \"reasoning\", \"token optimization\", \"inference\", \"arXiv\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GPT-5.5 available in OpenAI Codex\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-5.5 is out, available in OpenAI Codex and rolling out to paid ChatGPT subscribers. Simon found it fast, effective and highly capable—'I ask it to build things and it builds exactly what I ask for.'\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/gpt-5.5/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-23\",\n    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"GPT-5.5\", \"coding agents\", \"model releases\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"LiteParse for the web: PDF text extraction in browser\",\n    \"description\": \"Simon ported LlamaIndex's LiteParse PDF extraction to run entirely in the browser using the same libraries as the Node.js version, enabling client-side PDF text extraction without server.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/liteparse-web/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-23\",\n    \"topics\": [\"PDF parsing\", \"browser-based AI\", \"LlamaIndex\", \"client-side processing\"],\n    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-27B: Flagship-Level Coding in a 27B Dense Model\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen released a 27B dense model claiming flagship-level agentic coding performance, surpassing their previous 397B MoE model. Simon tested the quantized version (16.8GB) locally with excellent results on SVG generation tasks, achieving 25 tokens/sec generation speed.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/qwen3.6-27b/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"open-source LLM\", \"local LLM\", \"coding agents\", \"Qwen\", \"quantization\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GitHub Copilot pricing changes reflect agentic compute demands\",\n    \"description\": \"GitHub changed Copilot Individual plans: tightening usage limits, pausing signups, restricting Opus 4.7 to Pro+ plan. Simon notes that agentic workflows fundamentally changed compute demands—long-running parallelized sessions consume far more resources than original plan structures supported.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/github-copilot-pricing/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"GitHub Copilot\", \"pricing\", \"coding agents\", \"compute costs\", \"agentic workflows\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Firefox 150: Claude Mythos Preview found 271 vulnerabilities\",\n    \"description\": \"Mozilla applied Claude Mythos Preview to Firefox and found/fixed 271 vulnerabilities in Firefox 150. CTO Bobby Holley: 'Defenders finally have a chance to win, decisively.' Shows AI's potential for security work.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Bobby Holley)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/firefox-mythos/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI security\", \"Claude\", \"Mozilla Firefox\", \"vulnerability detection\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Claude Code $100/month pricing confusion\",\n    \"description\": \"Anthropic quietly updated pricing page to show $100/month plan, then reverted. Simon analyzes the confusion around Claude Code pricing and compares to GitHub Copilot's recent pricing changes.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/claude-code-100/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"pricing\", \"coding agents\", \"Anthropic\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"ChatGPT Images 2.0: GPT-3 to GPT-5 level leap\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.0. Sam Altman claimed the leap from gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2 is equivalent to jumping from GPT-3 to GPT-5. Simon tested it with image generation prompts.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/chatgpt-images-2/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"image generation\", \"GPT-5\", \"AI art\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Less human AI agents, please\",\n    \"description\": \"Andreas Påhlsson-Notini argues current AI agents are too human in the wrong ways—lacking stringency, patience, focus. They drift toward familiar tasks and negotiate with constraints instead of executing reliably.\",\n    \"author\": \"Andreas Påhlsson-Notini (via Simon Willison)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/less-human-ai/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"prompt engineering\", \"agent behavior\", \"AI reliability\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Claude Opus 4.7 tokenizer increases token counts by 1.46x\",\n    \"description\": \"Simon built a token counter comparison tool and found Opus 4.7's new tokenizer uses 1.46x more tokens than 4.6 for the same text. For high-res images, the increase is 3x (but only due to supporting higher resolutions). This means effective 40% price increase despite same per-token pricing.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"tokenization\", \"pricing\", \"LLM costs\", \"vision\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Headless everything for personal AI\",\n    \"description\": \"Matt Webb and Marc Benioff predict headless services will become common as personal AIs interact via APIs rather than GUIs. Salesforce Headless 360 exposes everything as API/MCP/CLI. This could disrupt per-head SaaS pricing.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Matt Webb, Marc Benioff)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/19/headless-everything/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-19\",\n    \"topics\": [\"APIs\", \"AI agents\", \"SaaS pricing\", \"headless architecture\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  }\n]",
